{"id":"mogemma-3hl","title":"PRD: Mojo GPU Standard Gemma Kernels","description":"North Star: implement CUDA-first non-MAX GPU execution for standard Gemma path in mogemma, including kernelization of core ops and device-resident cache handling with strict correctness parity and throughput tracking.","notes":"Chapters: gpu-standard-kernels_20260304, gpu-kv-cache-device-memory_20260304, gpu-standard-correctness-gates_20260304. Created by /flow:prd on 2026-03-04.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2026-03-04T23:36:45.062875763Z","created_by":"cody","updated_at":"2026-03-04T23:36:45.837899428Z","source_repo":".","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0}
{"id":"mogemma-h4n","title":"PRD: obstore to Mojo CFFI migration","description":"North Star: replace the current Python obstore-based model download path in HubManager.download() with a Rust-backed downloader exposed through Mojo CFFI, then hard-cut over with no backward compatibility path. This PRD exists to reduce Python-side storage overhead and move the data-plane closer to our Mojo runtime boundary while prioritizing download performance and reliability. Expected outcomes: (1) architecture and contract for Rust<->Mojo<->Python boundary, (2) migration plan that removes direct obstore usage from HubManager.download, (3) clear performance/reliability validation gates before removal of old path.","notes":"Chapters: obstore-cffi-architecture_20260302, rust-downloader-ffi-contract_20260302, hub-hard-cutover_20260302, perf-reliability-gates_20260302. Created by /flow:prd on 2026-03-02.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2026-03-02T03:31:00.414731566Z","created_by":"cody","updated_at":"2026-03-02T03:31:06.922738165Z","source_repo":".","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0}
{"id":"mogemma-h4n.1","title":"Flow: obstore-cffi-architecture_20260302","description":"Define target architecture and API contracts to replace HubManager.download obstore calls with Rust->Mojo CFFI data path. Deliverables: boundary contract, error model, and migration constraints for hard cutover.","notes":"Part of PRD: obstore-to-mojo-cffi_20260302. Chapter 1 of 4. Dependencies: none. Focus files: src/py/mogemma/hub.py, src/py/mogemma/model.py, src/mo/mogemma/core.mojo, src/py/tests/test_hub.py.\n\nRevision 2026-03-06: tightened the downloader architecture contract around ABI ownership, Python/Mojo compatibility guardrails, bounded concurrency defaults, and contract-verification/TDD evidence.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2026-03-02T03:31:15.965804702Z","created_by":"cody","updated_at":"2026-03-06T00:44:42.774791639Z","source_repo":".","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"mogemma-h4n.1","depends_on_id":"mogemma-h4n","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-03-02T03:31:15.965804702Z","created_by":"cody","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
